    <!--
        Phase B5 of the "Property Package -> Portfolio Deal" rename program (2026-08-18).

        Structural clone of flexipages/Property_Package_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml, which is
        deleted in this same wave (manifest/portfolio-deal-b5/destructiveChangesPost.xml). A
        FlexiPage's sobjectType is not editable in place, so retiring the object forces a new page
        rather than a repoint - that is why this file exists at all. Every region, facet, identifier,
        component and field reference is carried over unchanged; only <sobjectType> and <masterLabel>
        differ. The six data fields did NOT rename in this program, only the object did.

        VERIFIED DELIBERATE, NOT A TRANSCRIPTION GAP: this page was diffed against a freshly
        CLI-generated `sf template generate flexipage` run with the RecordPage template for
        Portfolio_Deal__c on 2026-08-18. (The CLI flag name is spelled out in prose here rather than
        quoted verbatim, deliberately: a literal double hyphen is ILLEGAL inside an XML comment body,
        and quoting the flag is what made an earlier revision of this file fail to parse at all. Do
        not "restore" the flag syntax. Same rule applies to every other CLI flag mentioned in any
        comment in this repo's metadata.) The generator emits three things this file intentionally
        does not have, all three inherited from the old page's own deliberate edits:
          1. a `Delete` entry in dynamicHighlights actionNames (and numVisibleActions 3, not 1);
          2. the sidebar region / activityTab / runtime_sales_activities:activityPanel block;
          3. a comment block ABOVE the root <FlexiPage> element - which on this project is a known
             deploy-breaker (`sf` fails at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
             matching parent xml file" error), so it is stripped, and this comment lives INSIDE the
             root instead.

        No sidebar / Activity tab: Portfolio_Deal__c, like the Property_Package__c it replaces, is
        created only by the Broker Protection pipeline and carries enableActivities=false on the
        object, so a runtime_sales_activities:activityPanel here would be a permanently-empty,
        non-functional tab. Omitted deliberately rather than shipped broken.

        This page has no CustomTab and is not assigned via a FlexiPage <flexiPageRegions> app
        assignment: it is reached solely through the Acquisition app's `View` actionOverride for
        pageOrSobjectType=Portfolio_Deal__c, added in this same wave. Removing that override is what
        makes a record page unreachable - which is exactly how the old page is being retired.
    -->
    <description></description>
    <masterLabel>Portfolio Deal Record Page</masterLabel>
    <sobjectType>Portfolio_Deal__c</sobjectType>
    <template>
